WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:05.210
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video I'll be explaining everything

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.050
you need to know about the ending to Venom
and how the various symbiotes in the movie

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.580
set up future sequels.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.309
Plus keep watching to the end where I'll reveal
some sneaky easter eggs and little details

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:18.699
you might have missed in the post-credits,
as well as the details of my new Venom giveaway.

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:22.640
In case you hadn't already guessed, of course,
I'll be talking spoilers, so take care if

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.830
you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:29.020
At the end of the film, Venom defeats Drake
and Riot by sabotaging their rocket launch

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.660
causing it to explode, and Venom initially
appears to perish during the flaming fallout

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.800
and says "Goodbye Eddie".

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.870
Eddie later has a reunion with Anne who believes
he's free of the symbiote, but it's revealed

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.700
that Venom's still alive and there talking
to Eddie in his head.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.700
Anne gets a little suspicious as she notices
Eddie appearing to talk to himself, but he

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.700
decides to not tell her yet.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.600
Eddie clearly wants to get back together with
her, and Venom chips in "You belong with us

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.900
Annie", a hint that we'll see She-Venom again
in the potential sequel – and I'll talk

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.469
more about Anne's She-Venom shortly.

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.360
Eddie decides to keep Venom's existence a
secret from Anne for the moment and this scene

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.429
reminded me of the end of the first Tobey
Maguire Spider-Man movie where Peter Parker

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:06.770
hides his feelings from Mary Jane, although
they eventually got together in the next movie.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:09.630
So, what's the future for Venom and his fellow
symbiotes?

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.750
Well, the ending sets up how Eddie and Venom
will interact with each other going forward.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.390
Earlier in the movie, we saw that often the
symbiotes will eat their human hosts from

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.250
the inside which seems to be why they keep
travelling from planet to planet devouring

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.340
their hosts until there aren't any left.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.090
Venom is a bit different from his fellow symbiotes
and he gains an appreciation for Earth after

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.579
he climbs up the skyscraper and looks out
over the city in a rather Spider-Man-esque

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:34.579
moment.

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:38.790
Although Venom started off forcing his host
Eddie to do whatever Venom wanted, by the

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:43.430
end of the movie, Eddie has found he can control
Venom more and quiet him down.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.100
Eddie also decides to teach Venom about right
and wrong and how he can't eat or hurt good

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.100
people.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.691
Venom needs to eat though, of course, otherwise
he'll end up eating Eddie's insides, and we

00:01:53.691 --> 00:01:57.920
discover Venom has a taste for Tater Tots
and chocolate when they go to the store for

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.920
food.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.420
Which leads to the scene where Venom eats
the thug who's been shaking down Mrs Chen.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.119
I guess this means that Eddie will have to
keep hunting down bad guys as a way to keep

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:07.570
Venom's hunger at bay!

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.470
As for Anne's future, there a big hint to
that in the scene where we discover she's

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.910
bonded with the Venom symbiote and has become
She-Venom.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.890
She saves Eddie as he's about to be killed
by Drake's henchmen, then makes out with him

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.080
at which point Venom flips from her back to
Eddie.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.230
Venom's reply of "Not today" when she demands
to join the fight against Riot is a tease

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:30.210
that She-Venom will be back for a much bigger
part in a possible Venom sequel.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:35.500
And, of course, Anne did end up fighting ugly,
as she put it, when she disabled Riot temporarily

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.230
during the Rocket launch sequence by turning
up the loudspeakers.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:43.411
The Venom sequel is also going to have an
even more powerful villain than Riot, which

00:02:43.411 --> 00:02:48.580
I'll explain next, and I think Eddie and Venom
will likely need Anne's She-Venom powers against

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.580
him.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.250
OK, so Venom's next villain is set up in the
first post-credits scene where we see Eddie

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.340
making his way to San Quentin Prison.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:00.060
As he mentioned previously to Anne, he's got
a job reporting again and has what he calls

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.590
the interview of a lifetime with serial killer
Cletus Kasady.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.590
In this scene, we finally meet Woody Harrelson
who has said that his tiny role in this film

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.690
sets him up for a much bigger part in a Venom
sequel.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.880
The prison guard calls Kasady "Red" a little
reference to the villain's red hair and the

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.450
red and black colour of the Carnage symbiote
which bonds with Kasady in the comics.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.500
As Kasady talks to Eddie, he threatens that
when he gets out of prison there'll be carnage,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:28.010
a very on-the-nose nod to the fact we'll be
seeing Kasady become a host for the Carnage

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.860
symbiote in the next movie.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:34.330
In the comics, Eddie Brock and Cletus Kasady
end up sharing time in prison together, something

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:38.490
the movie alludes to by the fact that the
imprisoned Kasady asked specifically for Eddie

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.900
to interview him.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.550
In the books, Kasady became Carnage when Eddie's
pregnant symbiote gave birth and the spawn

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.410
attached itself to Cletus.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:51.060
In the film, Eddie told Venom to keep quiet
during the visit and I didn't see any hint

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.620
of the symbiote leaking out during what we
saw of Eddie's time there.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.400
So, unless Kasady's already been exposed to
a symbiote off screen, how will he end up

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.400
as Carnage?

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.350
Well, we need to recap what symbiotes are
still left by the end of the Venom movie and

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.500
how Kasady will be exposed to one.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:11.120
The LIFE Foundation extracted 4 distinct symbiote
samples from the comet.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.050
There was the black one, Venom, who currently
inhabits Eddie.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.760
There was a blue one and a yellow one and
each of those died in the movie when their

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.930
hosts died, one of which was Jenny Slate's
character, Dr Dora Skirth.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.160
The fourth sample was Riot, the symbiote which
escaped after the LIFE Foundation's space

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.050
craft crashed in Malaysia.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:32.250
Riot hopped around from host to host passing
from the EMT technician, to the old woman

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.040
in the market, then to the little girl at
the airport and finally on to Drake.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.120
But Riot died together with Drake during the
rocket explosion; remember there are just

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:45.800
two things which can kill a symbiote: fire
and a sustained sound above a certain frequency.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.200
What's even more important to recall though
is that there are millions of other symbiotes

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.360
still on that comet that is presumably passing
through or near our Solar System.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.540
And debris that breaks off from comets often
ends up as meteorites when they fall into

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.540
the Earth's atmosphere.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:02.710
What if a red symbiote fell to Earth via a
meteor?

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.050
It might even crash-land in San Quentin prison
and help Cletus Kasady escape!

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.310
By the way, in the comics, Carnage is such
a powerful villain that Venom has typically

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.790
teamed up with Spider-Man and the Fantastic
Four to combat the evil symbiote.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.560
At the moment, Sony's deal with Marvel Studios
means Spider-Man can only appear in the MCU,

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:25.230
not any of Sony's current films; however,
after Avengers 4 and Spider-Man: Far From

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:29.940
Home, Tom Holland's Peter Parker will have
appeared in 5 MCU movies and it's possible

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.020
that Sony could pull Spider-Man back into
their own Marvel Universe to appear in a Venom

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.020
sequel.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.420
Bonus easter egg time now: The way Kasady
writes 'Welcome Eddie' in blood inside his

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:44.190
cage is a little hat-tip to how his character
leaves the phrase 'Carnage Rules' in various

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.920
places in the comics.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.280
If you didn't manage to stay all the way through
the very long and pretty slow-moving credits,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.120
you probably missed the second end-credits
scene which was a tease for Sony's animated

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.510
Spider-Man Into The Spider-Verse movie.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:06:01.260
The scene begins with a comic-book pop-up
graphic "Meanwhile in another universe" indicating

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.240
that the animated movie exists in a different
reality to the Venom movie.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.560
What we see next is not a trailer, but a full-length
scene.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.370
The animation on show looks fantastic, however,
because it doesn't have any impact on Venom

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:18.900
or any future Venom sequel, it feels a little
disconnected so it's basically just an extended

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.900
advert.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.110
Of course, Marvel has simply shown scenes
from upcoming movies as post-credit scenes,

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:28.360
however, they do all exist within the same
universe so it doesn't feel quite as odd.

